Optimisations of the MZ77 codec
===============================

One file per optimisation, in the order they were applied.  Each says
what changed, why it should help, how correctness was checked, and what
the measurements showed.  The measurements themselves, with every raw
log, are in bench/log/MACHINE/STEP/; bench/log/MACHINE/SUMMARY.md puts
all steps side by side.

  11-block-io.md          #11  block I/O instead of a call per byte
  12-inline-bitio.md      #12  inline bit reader and writer
  14-no-memmove.md        #14  one buffer for window and look-ahead
  15-compare-8-bytes.md   #15  compare 8 bytes at a time in the match loop
  16-avx512bw.md          #16  AVX-512BW match compare (Intel Tiger Lake)
  avx2.md                      AVX2 match compare (AMD Zen 2)
  13-lto-pgo.md           #13  link-time and profile-guided optimisation

The archive format never changes: every step produces archives that are
byte-identical to the original program's (raw/archives.sha256 in every
step, compared in SUMMARY.md).
